findings.description:
D3 rejects a candidate with `no_slice_plan_at_fork` when `plan_file_for` finds no plan "at the fork". The data flow runs this check before any sandbox is created (line 116, before line 118). But the slice gives the signature as `plan_file_for(index, root)` (line 66), which reads a directory on disk, not a commit.

At that point only the user's checkout is available, and it is at today's HEAD. Reading it there would check the wrong revision. The slice needs to choose one of these:
- add a git-based variant that reads from `git ls-tree` / `git show`, as D3 already does for the design and task files;
- move the check after the fork sandbox is created;
- extract the fork tree to a temporary directory first.

Whichever is chosen is another interface change and belongs in the list from the previous finding. Note that `CfRegistration` also calls `plan_file_for` (D9), but there it runs inside the sandbox tree, so it is fine.
